  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;</p><p>Number of turns per metre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1200</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Magnetic field at centre inside the solenoid is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>nI</mi></math>,&nbsp;where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the permeability constant.</p><p>Magnetic intensity is related to magnetic field by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1200</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
